 Looks like it's `like` expr bug:

    drop table if exists t0;
    create table t0(col1 varchar(255));
    insert into t0 values("\\9jM\\M");
    select 1 from t0 where t0.col1 like t0.col1;

TiDB master: 

    mysql> select 1 from t0 where t0.col1 like t0.col1;
    +---+
    | 1 |
    +---+
    | 1 |
    +---+
    1 row in set (0.00 sec)

MySQL8.0:

    mysql> select 1 from t0 where t0.col1 like t0.col1;
    Empty set (0.01 sec)
